# c32 -- Fekete's read-only anomaly, with T3 declared read-only.
#
# c07 with T3 begun read-only. T3 begins after T1's commit, so
# T1, the T3 of the dangerous structure T3 --rw--> T2 --rw--> T1,
# committed before T3's snapshot: the declaration excuses
# nothing, and T3's snapshot is never safe while T2 runs. At S+S
# not all three may commit, as in c07.


== pairing RR/RR == T1=RR T2=RR T3=RR-RO
@1 T2 begin -> ok
@2 T2 read R1 -> 0
@2 T2 read R2 -> 0
@3 T1 begin -> ok
@4 T1 write R1 20 -> ok
@5 T1 commit -> ok
@6 T3 begin -> ok
@7 T3 read R1 -> 20
@7 T3 read R2 -> 0
@8 T3 commit? -> recorded
@9 T2 write R2 -12 -> ok
@10 T2 commit? -> recorded
@11 check committed T1 T2 T3 -> satisfied
== pairing RR/S == T1=RR T2=SER T3=SER-RO
@1 T2 begin -> ok
@2 T2 read R1 -> 0
@2 T2 read R2 -> 0
@3 T1 begin -> ok
@4 T1 write R1 20 -> ok
@5 T1 commit -> ok
@6 T3 begin -> ok
@7 T3 read R1 -> 20
@7 T3 read R2 -> 0
@8 T3 commit? -> recorded
@9 T2 write R2 -12 -> ok
@10 T2 commit? -> recorded
@11 check committed T1 T2 T3 -> satisfied
== pairing S/RR == T1=SER T2=RR T3=RR-RO
@1 T2 begin -> ok
@2 T2 read R1 -> 0
@2 T2 read R2 -> 0
@3 T1 begin -> ok
@4 T1 write R1 20 -> ok
@5 T1 commit -> ok
@6 T3 begin -> ok
@7 T3 read R1 -> 20
@7 T3 read R2 -> 0
@8 T3 commit? -> recorded
@9 T2 write R2 -12 -> ok
@10 T2 commit? -> recorded
@11 check committed T1 T2 T3 -> satisfied
== pairing S/S == T1=SER T2=SER T3=SER-RO
@1 T2 begin -> ok
@2 T2 read R1 -> 0
@2 T2 read R2 -> 0
@3 T1 begin -> ok
@4 T1 write R1 20 -> ok
@5 T1 commit -> ok
@6 T3 begin -> ok
@7 T3 read R1 -> 20
@7 T3 read R2 -> 0
@8 T3 commit? -> recorded
@9 T2 write R2 -12 -> ok
@10 T2 commit? -> recorded
@11 check not-all-committed T1 T2 T3 -> satisfied
